{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:36:13.264Z","data":{"text":"I completed task 1. Summary of what was done and verified:\n\n**Implementation** (`crates/kernel/specs/src/validate/`)\n- `finding.rs` — public `SpecFinding` (code, file, line, requirement, message, fix) and `FindingCode` with all eighteen kebab-case codes, `as_str`, `fix`, and serde renaming; `SpecFinding::new` takes its fix from the code.\n- `outline.rs` — a normalized-line scan giving each `##` heading its line/title and each requirement block its header line, parsed `Requirement`, scenario lines and heading-section index.\n- `requirement.rs` — whole-word SHALL/MUST outside fences, missing-scenario, per-scenario WHEN/THEN, and duplicate-scenario rules.\n- `living.rs` — `validate_living_spec` and `validate_living_specs` (byte-order folder walk, missing folder = no finding, unreadable `spec.md` = naming read error).\n- `lib.rs` re-exports; fixtures copied byte-for-byte.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/validating_living.rs` — Finding codes (all 18 rows: code, fix, serialization), Living spec findings, Requirement findings.\n- `tests/validating_living_rules.rs` — Whole-word keywords, an ordering/all-four-delta-headings case, Living specs folder.\n\n**Verification**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --test validating_living` green.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` exits 0 (fmt, workspace clippy with `-D warnings`, all tests, corpus included).\n- `cargo mutants` over the four new source files: 49 caught, 7 unviable, no miss, no timeout.\n- A temporary scratch check (deleted) confirmed this repository's living specs validate with no finding.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/217-rust-specs-validate/.run/results/1.md`."}}
